From df5257e2f78a25ac0eebc689df733199adef6d94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 22:29:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] revdi: expose an owned Rust client API

Keep the C ABI for DisplayLinkManager compatibility while giving Rust clients a safe owner for device handles, event callbacks, registered scanout storage, damage, and teardown. Switch Chimera to that API, unregister buffers before replacing their storage, and honor immediately-ready update requests.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-0
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
